 "final_summary": "The root cause was that the `load_config` function in `tracker/config.py` failed to handle malformed JSON files, raising a `JSONDecodeError` instead of falling back to default values. The fix added proper exception handling for `JSONDecodeError` in the `_read_file` function, ensuring malformed config files are ignored and defaults are used. This satisfies the API contract and prevents startup crashes.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/config.py b/tracker/config.py\nindex d17fed6..e65d2a7 100644\n--- a/tracker/config.py\n+++ b/tracker/config.py\n@@ -54,11 +54,10 @@ def _read_file(path):\n     try:\n         with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as handle:\n             data = json.load(handle)\n-    except OSError:\n+    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError):\n         return {}\n     return data if isinstance(data, dict) else {}\n \n-\n def load_config(overrides=None, env=None, config_file=None):\n     env = os.environ if env is None else env\n     overrides = overrides or {}\n",
